raye-settings (0.5~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New For developers section in System > Advanced: Developer Mode,
    Device Portal (a web page to manage this PC from the local network,
    with pairing, sessions and a connection log), device discovery and
    OpenSSH with keys only.
  * Menus, drop-down lists, flyouts and tooltips are solid again, and
    "..." menus open with nothing picked.
  * No Wi-Fi card: no Wi-Fi, Known networks or Mobile hotspot pages, and
    the network pages stop mentioning Wi-Fi. A USB Wi-Fi key plugged in
    brings them back.
  * Password prompts ask for root access; account types are Sudo user
    and Standard user.
  * Going back to the point before an update no longer installs that
    update again.
  * Install now says when it waits for the charger: "Plug in your PC to
    install these updates."
  * Greyed-out settings are easier to read, and the placeholder, night
    light, AutoPlay and app list pages are tidier.
  * A newer background choice is kept when a video finishes converting.
  * American spelling in page names, summaries and messages.
  * A Windows program's page says which profile it runs with: Optimized
    for Raye, or Default.
  * Restart, Shut down and End task in Device Portal take the sudo
    password typed in the page; no prompt shows up on the PC instead.
  * Sounds and Controllers are Raye pages now: pick and hear the sound
    scheme, turn event sounds off, see each controller and try its
    buttons and sticks.
  * Virus & threat protection shows the firewall, security updates, Store
    apps and Windows programs and how each stands, instead of a
    placeholder.
  * New switch in For developers: debug messages of Windows programs.
  * On a PC without Wi-Fi the Network tile says "Ethernet, VPN, proxy".
  * Rows for features Raye doesn't have (dynamic lighting, widgets,
    casting, mono audio, voice typing) and the More accessibility options
    module are gone; Email & accounts only shows when an account service
    is installed.
  * Device security: turn device encryption on or off with the PC on,
    with its progress, a recovery key shown once (save it to a file or
    print it), the Secure Boot steps with a restart into the firmware
    settings, and the TPM version.
  * Sound has a switch for the sound played when you change the volume,
    and the Volume slider plays it when you let go.
  * Encryption progress reads "50%" in English.
  * Identify shows one number on each screen, in its bottom left corner,
    for three seconds; clicking again no longer stacks a second one. The
    line under your name says Standard user for a non-sudo account.
  * Device security shows the disk as encrypted as soon as the
    background run ends, without opening the page again.

 -- techoraye <190692880+techoraye@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:42:05 +0000

raye-settings (0.3~beta1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Raye Update marks each update that needs a restart, offers Install
    now when none does, and shows the install progress.
  * Firmware that is already up to date is listed as up to date, and
    raye-kernel no longer counts as a second kernel.
  * Recovery: restore points are named after what made them, Create a
    restore point is one click away, and Go back shows on a real
    install.
  * Personalization > Background can show an animation, Raye's or your
    own GIF, MP4 or WebM. A video is trimmed once to 30 frames a second
    and 1080 lines.
  * The background type no longer says "Picture" when a slideshow is on.
  * Calmer greys, with the navigation tiles and page glyphs in the flat
    accent colour.

