raye-settings (0.1~dev5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Raye Update page: pause updates for one to five weeks, and resume.
  * Opening a page directly (raye-settings raye:update) selects its
    category in the side bar.
  * Raye Settings answers for KDE System Settings: Plasma's "Configure..."
    links and the settings KRunner finds open it on the same module; KDE's
    window leaves the menu and stays one click away as "Advanced settings".
  * Drivers page: a Raye kernel card to switch to it or back, with the
    one-time code to type at the key enrollment screen.
  * The Raye kernel card follows the trial boot: it says when a restart
    tries the kernel (and that an encrypted disk asks for its password
    that one time), and offers to try again if it did not start.

